
mem 63 gb

(  CALCULATION OF VIBRATION ENERGIES FOR ABCD MOLECULE )
(  NH3, fitted to points PES                           )
(  2014,  EXAMPLE of J=0                               )

KinOrder  6   (Max order in the kinetic energy expansion)
PotOrder  8   (Max order in the potential energy expansion)

Natoms 4       (Number of atoms)
Nmodes 6       (Number of modes = 3*Natoms-6)

(ACTIVE SPACE CUTOFFS:)
PRIMITIVES
  Npolyads       34         (how many polyads we calculate)
  enercut        40000.      (energy cut in the primitive matrix for the diagonalization)
END

CONTRACTION
  Npolyads       34          (how many polyads we calculate)
  enercut       100000.      (energy cut in the primitive matrix for the diagonalization)
  degeneracy   1e-2
  sample_points  40
  sample_attempts 500
  symm_toler      1e-3
  coeff_thresh    1e-16
  model j=0
END

verbose 4

DIAGONALIZER
 SYEV     (syev-default, syevr - optional, nroots or uplimit can be given)
end


dstep 0.001,0.001,0.001,0.01,0.01,0.01     (finite difference element for each mode )
COORDS     linear (type of the internal coordinates: linear or local)
TRANSFORM  R-S-DELTA ( xi(chi): normal, linear, r-s-delta, r-s-rho, r-alpha-tau, see molecule.f90)
MOLTYPE    XY3    (Identifying type of the Molecule (e.g. XY3))
MOLECULE   NH3    (Identifying the Molecule, e.g. PH3, BiH3 - optional)
REFER-CONF NON-RIGID  (Reference configuarion: RIGID or NON-RIGID)

SYMGROUP D3h(M)

ZMAT
    N   0  0  0  0  14.00307401
    H   1  0  0  0   1.00782505
    H   1  2  0  0   1.00782505
    H   1  2  3  1   1.00782505
end


CHECK_POINT
hamiltonian read
external none
contract read
eigenfunc none
matelem convert split 13  13
extmatelem none
END

BASIS
